---
// Sec. 03, after the Linux machines: the agents on one phone as a crew.
// They pass notes (Agent messages: the floor plan and its key), take turns
// on the one screen (the queue) and keep working while you're away (the
// long shift).
import FloorPlan from "./crew/FloorPlan.astro";
import Levels from "./crew/Levels.astro";
import Queue from "./crew/Queue.astro";
import Shift from "./crew/Shift.astro";
---

<section class="section crew" id="crew">
    <div class="sec-head">
        <div class="sec-rail">
            <p class="kicker">Sec. 03 / Agent messages</p>
            <p class="fig-label">FIG. 05 — Floor plan</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sec-body">
            <h2>Pass notes. Take turns. Pull all-nighters.</h2>
            <p class="lead">
                Every agent on your phone can message the others, one at a
                time or all at once, and wake one that's idle to answer.
                They line up for the one screen, share a machine when you
                let them, and keep working after you put the phone down.{" "}
                <em>The runner on the phone carries every note: no server, no cloud in between.</em>
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <FloorPlan />
    <Levels />

    <div class="crew-pair">
        <div class="crew-fig">
            <p class="fig-label">FIG. 05B — Now serving</p>
            <h3>One screen. One driver.</h3>
            <p>
                An agent that asks while another drives gets its place in
                line, the driver hears who's waiting, and the next one hears
                when it's free. A turn another agent's note started can't
                take the screen: phone control stays with work you started.
            </p>
            <Queue />
        </div>
        <div class="crew-fig">
            <p class="fig-label">FIG. 05C — The long shift</p>
            <h3>Built to run all night.</h3>
            <p>
                Agents keep working with the app in the background and the
                screen off, with no clock running out on them.
            </p>
            <Shift />
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<style is:global>
    .crew-pair {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: clamp(28px, 4vw, 48px);
      margin-top: clamp(48px, 6vw, 72px);
    }
    .crew-fig { display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-width: 0; }
    .crew-fig h3 {
      margin-top: 12px;
      font: 400 clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px)/1 var(--serif);
      letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    }
    .crew-fig > p:not(.fig-label) {
      max-width: 52ch;
      margin: 10px 0 22px;
      font-size: 14px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: var(--muted);
    }
    .crew-fig > figure { flex: 1; }

    @media (max-width: 980px) {
      .crew-pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
</style>
